        {
          "say": "That is not unusual. Small experiments can be far from theory."
        },
        {
          "say": "Happened over tried. It is also called experimental probability.",
          "write": "experimental probability"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "More trials, better estimates",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Here is one coin experiment, tossed again and again.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y7/maths/experiments-and-relative-frequency-trials.svg",
          "alt": "Relative frequency of heads getting closer to 0.5"
        },
        {
          "say": "After 10 tosses, 0.7. After 100 tosses, 0.47.",
          "write": "10: 0.7   100: 0.47"
        },
        {
          "say": "After 500 tosses, 0.502. Very close to one half.",
          "write": "500: 0.502"
        },
        {
          "say": "More trials usually bring you closer to the theory.",
          "write": "more trials, more trust"
        },
        {
          "say": "A drawing pin has no simple theory. So an experiment is the best estimate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "A coin tossed 50 times",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A coin lands heads 28 times in 50 tosses.",
          "write": "28 heads in 50"
        },
        {
          "say": "Relative frequency of heads is 28 over 50, which is 0.56.",
          "write": "28/50 = 0.56"
        },
        {
          "say": "Tails happened 22 times. That is 0.44.",
          "write": "22/50 = 0.44"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check: 0.56 plus 0.44 is one. Close to one half each.",
          "write": "0.56 + 0.44 = 1 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Making predictions",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Expected number equals probability times number of trials.",
          "write": "expected = P × trials"
        },
        {
          "say": "Roll a fair die 60 times. Expect one sixth of 60, which is 10 sixes.",
          "write": "1/6 × 60 = 10"
        },
        {
          "say": "We actually got 14 sixes. That happens by chance quite often.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y7/maths/experiments-and-relative-frequency-ex2.svg",
          "alt": "Column graph of 60 die rolls with dashed line at 10"
        },
        {
          "say": "A pin lands point up 130 times in 200. That is 0.65.",
          "write": "130/200 = 0.65"
        },
        {
          "say": "In 1000 drops, expect about 650 point up.",
          "write": "0.65 × 1000 = 650"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Is it fair?",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A spinner has 4 equal sections. Expect red a quarter of the time.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y7/maths/experiments-and-relative-frequency-ex4.svg",
          "alt": "Spinner with four equal sections"
        },
        {
          "say": "In 40 spins, expect 10 reds.",
          "write": "1/4 × 40 = 10",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 180,
            "alt": "Expected 10 reds",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "expected 10"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "It landed on red 26 times. Far more than 10.",
          "write": "26/40 = 0.65",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 180,
            "alt": "Actual 26 reds is much more than 10 expected",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "expected 10"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 416,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "actual 26"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So there is evidence the spinner may be biased. Spin it more to be sure.",
          "write": "may be biased"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Divide by the number of trials, not the number of faces.",
          "write": "RF = ÷ trials"
        },
        {
          "say": "Results are close to theory, not exactly the same.",
          "write": "close, not exact"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't call something biased after only a few trials.",
          "write": "few trials = weak evidence"
        },
        {
          "say": "After five tails, a coin is not due a head. Coins have no memory.",
          "write": "P(head) still 1/2"
        },
        {
          "say": "Say about 650, not exactly 650.",
          "write": "about 650"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Relative frequency is happened over tried.",
          "write": "RF = happened ÷ tried"
        },
        {
          "say": "More trials give better estimates.",
          "write": "more trials, more trust"
        },
        {
          "say": "Expected number is probability times trials.",
          "write": "expected = P × trials"
        },
        {
          "say": "Dice have no memory. Each roll starts fresh.",
          "write": "no memory"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}